<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">ANNUAL APPEAL CONTRIBUTORS: OUR APOLOGIES</div>
  <p>In the spring issue, The Crosby Arboretum expressed our sincere gratitude to the persons and businesses for their generous contributions to our 2012 Annual Appeal. We sincerely apologize for the oversight in the previous issue, where we inadvertently omitted from the list. We extend our belated appreciation to Charles C. Lynch, V. Cox, Robert L. Davis, Shirley Muhleslen, Robert & Cynthia Murcison, Picayune Civic Women's Club, and others who contributed to our success.</p>

  <div class="two-column-layout">
    <div class="column">
      <div class="sub-heading">MEMORIAL TREES PLANTED</div>
      <p>Trees were planted at the Crosby Arboretum this winter and spring in memory of <span data-field="memorial_donor_1">{{ memorial_donor_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="memorial_donor_2">{{ memorial_donor_2 }}</span>, <span data-field="memorial_donor_3">{{ memorial_donor_3 }}</span>, and <span data-field="memorial_donor_4">{{ memorial_donor_4 }}</span>. In addition, trees were planted in memory of <span data-field="memorial_donor_5">{{ memorial_donor_5 }}</span>, <span data-field="memorial_donor_6">{{ memorial_donor_6 }}</span>, <span data-field="memorial_donor_7">{{ memorial_donor_7 }}</span>, and <span data-field="memorial_donor_8">{{ memorial_donor_8 }}</span>. Information on Memorial and Honor Trees, including a list of donors, can be found on the Arboretum website.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="image-container">
        <img src="placeholder_image_4.jpg" alt="Arboretum scene">
        <p class="caption">Mississippi Gulf Coast National Heritage Area Kiosk. (Image by <span data-field="image_credit_3">{{ image_credit_3 }}</span>)</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sub-heading">MISSISSIPPI GULF COAST NATIONAL HERITAGE AREA KIOSK</div>
      <p>The Crosby Arboretum has been selected as one of 17 sites to house a web-based Mississippi Gulf Coast National Heritage Area (MGCNHA) kiosk. This kiosk provides information on trails (hiking and kayaking), history, and culture of the area. The kiosk is located in the area. Funding for the kiosk was made possible through a grant from the Mississippi Department of Marine Resources (MDMR). The MGCNHA is managed through the MDMR. The kiosk is located at the MGCNHA site, which identifies the cultural and natural resources that contribute to the fabric of our national history and identity. The Crosby Arboretum embodies the mission of the MGCNHA, celebrating our region's unique landscapes, history, people, and traditions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

